# Homepage Redesign – Section-wise UI/UX Improvements

### 1. Header & Navigation

The header has been redesigned with a cleaner and more organized layout to improve navigation and usability. Compared to the previous Wix design, the new navigation features better spacing, a modern sticky header, and a more prominent call-to-action button. These improvements make it easier for visitors to navigate the website while giving the homepage a more professional and premium appearance.

### 2. Hero Section

The hero section has been completely refreshed to create a stronger first impression. Instead of a simple static banner, the new design uses a full-width image carousel with a dark overlay, bold typography, and clear call-to-action buttons. This helps communicate the organization's mission more effectively while increasing user engagement from the moment visitors land on the homepage.

### 3. Mission / Focus Section

The mission section has been redesigned using modern information cards with icons, improved spacing, and a clear visual hierarchy. Breaking the content into individual cards makes the information easier to scan and understand, allowing visitors to quickly identify the organization's key goals and areas of focus.

### 4. Podcast Section

A dedicated podcast section has been introduced with a modern card-based design and premium styling. This provides greater visibility for podcast content, making it more attractive and accessible to visitors while encouraging them to explore the organization's media and thought leadership.

### 5. Events Section

The events section has been redesigned using visually appealing event cards that include images, event categories, dates, and action buttons. This organized layout allows users to browse upcoming events more easily and improves the overall presentation of event-related content.

### 6. Reports & Publications

The reports section now presents publications using modern content cards with featured images and improved typography. This makes research reports easier to discover and read while creating a more professional presentation that strengthens the organization's credibility.

### 7. Blog Section

The blog section has been updated with a clean card layout that highlights featured images, article titles, and summaries. The improved spacing and typography create a better reading experience and encourage visitors to explore more articles and stay engaged with the website's latest content.

### 8. Call-to-Action (CTA)

The homepage now includes a dedicated call-to-action section designed to encourage user engagement. With a strong headline, attractive background, and prominent action button, this section helps guide visitors toward important actions such as joining, contacting, or learning more about the organization.

### 9. Footer

The footer has been redesigned with a more structured layout that organizes navigation links, contact information, and social media icons into clear sections. This improves accessibility, enhances the overall user experience, and provides visitors with easy access to important resources from any page.

### Overall UI/UX Improvements

The new homepage focuses on creating a modern, responsive, and user-centered experience. Compared to the previous Wix design, the updated interface features improved visual hierarchy, better spacing, consistent typography, interactive components, and a cleaner overall layout. These enhancements not only improve the website's appearance but also make navigation more intuitive, increase user engagement, and provide a stronger digital presence for the organization.






